--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- NYLON mooring with LOAD-DEPENDENT dynamic stiffness (viscoelastic, ElasticMod 3)
-- Nylon (and polyester) show a dynamic stiffness that RISES with the mean load. MoorDyn's
-- ElasticMod 3 captures this: the EA column is three bar-parts `Es|alphaMBL|vbeta` -- the static
-- stiffness Es, the intercept alphaMBL (must exceed Es), and the mean-load coefficient vbeta;
-- the dynamic modulus Ed(T_mean) is recovered in closed form each step. The BA column is the
-- `Bs|Bd` dashpot pair (non-negative N-s). Nylon-representative soft rope; the softer EA also
-- makes the static catenary solve more forgiving. Grounded semi-taut geometry.
